# React Patterns

## Structure

- DRY: render repeated UI from arrays with `.map()` instead of copy-paste JSX
- Pass props explicitly (e.g. `title`, `excerpt`, `author`) - avoid `{ article }` object props
- Extract long Tailwind strings into class constant objects (e.g. `articleCardClasses`)
- Keep page-level components in `src/pages/*` and reusable components in `src/components/*`
- write code with these quality: DRY (Don’t Repeat Yourself), High Cohesion, Loose Coupling, Single Responsibility Principle (SRP)

## Beginner-Friendly Code

- Prefer code a beginner React student can follow over clever abstractions.
- Use clear names like `selectedCategory`, `onSelectCategory`, `isMenuOpen`, and `setIsMenuOpen`.
- When wrapping shadcn/Radix primitives, expose only the pieces currently used by the app.
- Add short comments for wrapper components that hide complex library behavior (e.g. Root, Trigger, Content, Item).
- Avoid adding generic helpers, custom hooks, or large config objects unless they remove real repetition.
- Keep state flow visible: define `useState` near the page or component that owns the behavior, then pass values/functions down as props.

## Conditional Classes

Prefer `if/else` over ternary for conditional class names:

```jsx
let tabClass = "rounded-full px-4 py-2 text-sm";
if (isActive) {
  tabClass += " bg-neutral-900 text-white";
} else {
  tabClass += " text-neutral-600 hover:bg-neutral-100";
}
```

## Variants

Use a `variant` prop for responsive or layout differences (e.g. `variant="desktop"` | `"mobile"`).

## Components

- Use shadcn/ui primitives from `@/components/ui/*` before writing custom elements
- Use `Button`, `Input`, etc. with CVA variants where applicable
